1
00:00:00,213 --> 00:00:01,383
(Leonard:)Why don't I just start?

2
00:00:02,715 --> 00:00:05,925
(Leonard:)Sometimes people have trouble
accepting accolades...

3
00:00:06,094 --> 00:00:09,934
(Leonard:)...if on a subconscious level,
they don't feel they deserve them.

4
00:00:10,098 --> 00:00:12,558
(Leonard:)Do you think maybe
that's what's happening here?

5
00:00:12,725 --> 00:00:14,605
(Sheldon:)Really, Leonard?

6
00:00:16,229 --> 00:00:20,019
You just going to try to recycle Adler's
doctrine of the inferiority complex?

7
00:00:20,191 --> 00:00:22,941
(Sheldon:)I could probably get that
from the woman at Ralph's.

8
00:00:23,111 --> 00:00:26,611
(Sheldon:)And she'd let me taste some pieces
of cheese for free.

9
00:00:26,781 --> 00:00:29,951
(Leonard:)But it could be part of your problem.
Let me give you an example.

10
00:00:30,118 --> 00:00:34,748
When I was 8, I won a ribbon
at the science fair for my project...

11
00:00:34,914 --> 00:00:37,954
(Leonard:)...Do Lima Beans Grow Better
to Classical Music.

12
00:00:38,126 --> 00:00:41,086
(Leonard:)But my mother pointed out
that it was just a rehash...

13
00:00:41,254 --> 00:00:42,634
(Leonard:)...of my brother's earlier...

14
00:00:42,797 --> 00:00:45,507
(Leonard:)...Do Lima Beans Grow Worse
to Rock 'n' Roll.

15
00:00:47,385 --> 00:00:50,925
(Leonard:)I felt so guilty
I gave the ribbon back.

16
00:00:51,097 --> 00:00:54,027
(Sheldon:)And how did that make you feel?

